  "notes": "REGISTER:\nThis is a rough, derogatory word. It's often used when the speaker is angry or dismissive of what someone else is saying. Common in confrontational speech and media.\n\nUSAGE:\n・〜をほざく - to spout/babble (something)\n・ほざくな - shut up, stop spouting nonsense\n・{何|なに}をほざいている - what are you blabbering about\n\nCOMPARISON:\n・ほざく - to babble, mouth off (derogatory)\n・{言|い}う - to say (neutral)\n・しゃべる - to talk, chat (casual)\n・{吠|ほ}える - to bark, to yell (also derogatory when about speech)\n\nNOTE:\nVery informal and can be considered rude. Mostly heard in fiction, arguments, or when expressing strong irritation.",
